    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0800" n="786" xml:id="pg786"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Boutwell, Secretary
                        of the Treasury, to Mr. Fish, Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 18,
                        1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Respectfully referring to your
                    communication of the 13th instant, and my reply thereto of the 14th, I have the
                    honor to transmit herewith a copy of a letter from the collector of customs at
                    New York, dated the 15th instant, stating that he had refused a clearance to the
                    steamer Columbia, (Quaker City,) because of suspicious circumstances connected
                    with her.</p>
                <p><seg type="margin">[57]</seg> *I am, very respectully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. S. BOUTWELL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                            Treasury.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton Fish</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d369-a1.xml" xpointer="d369-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
